-- Plate layout: a scientist submits an experiment design — the conditions to
-- test, a container type, how many containers, how many replicates — and the
-- software lays out every container and every well. The twelfth Velle spec,
-- written to stress one question against a domain that needs it: many records
-- from one request. A creation statement creates one record and a rule fires
-- once per record, so a request carrying counts, or a product of sets, had no
-- spelling until `for each` (Reference §14).
--
-- What the domain asks of the language, and where each answer lives:
--   · one request, many records — a `for each` block in the rule body runs
--     its statements once per element of each source, nested for a product:
--     containers × replicates containers, and under each the wells
--     (Reference §14, "Creating one record per element")
--   · a number as a set — the range `from 1 to n`, both ends included, the
--     one place a number becomes a set, legal only as a `for each` source
--   · a tree of created records — the container is named with `as` and its
--     wells point at it, all in one firing (Reference §14, "Naming the record
--     a statement creates")
--   · the conditions arrive with the design — `with conditions`, so they are
--     records a block can run over (Reference §6, "Inline part creation")
--   · the whole layout lands or is refused as one — every created container
--     and well is an entrant of the design's transaction, so one refused well
--     refuses the design (Reference §20, "All-or-nothing batches")
--   · the counts as readable facts — derivations over the laid-out records,
--     never a stored tally
--
-- Comment convention (as in payments.velle): plain comments tell the business
-- story; `velle:` comments note the language machinery on show.

-- ── Reference data ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- A kind of plate: how many wells it carries.
act ContainerType {
    name: text
    wellsPerContainer: integer
}

-- ── The request ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- One submission. The conditions arrive with it; the containers and wells are
-- what the spec lays out from it.
-- velle: `with conditions` — the conditions are parts of the design's closure,
-- so the design and its conditions land as one commit (Reference §6)
act ExperimentDesign {
    containerType: one ContainerType
    containerCount: integer
    replicates: integer
    -- each condition occupies a block of this many wells on every container
    wellsPerCondition: integer
    laidOutContainers: integer = count(containers)
    laidOutWells: integer = sum(containers, wellCount)
} with conditions

-- A value to test, and which block of wells holds it on every container.
shape Condition {
    design: one ExperimentDesign
    block: integer
    value: decimal
}

-- ── What the spec lays out ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

shape Container {
    design: one ExperimentDesign
    replicate: integer
    position: integer
    wellCount: integer = count(wells)
}

shape Well {
    container: one Container
    position: integer
    condition: one Condition
}

-- ── The books rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- A design with nothing to test, or nothing to lay out, is a mistake.
never (ExperimentDesign where count(conditions) == 0)
never (ExperimentDesign where containerCount < 1 or replicates < 1)

-- The blocks fill the plate exactly: conditions × wells per condition is the
-- container type's well count.
never (ExperimentDesign where wellsPerCondition * count(conditions) != containerType.wellsPerContainer)

-- Every condition names a block the plate has.
never (Condition where block < 1 or block > count(design.conditions))

-- ── The layout ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- "When a design is submitted, lay out every container and every well."
-- velle: the outer block runs once per replicate per position and names the
-- container it creates; the inner block runs once per condition per slot in
-- the condition's block, and each well points at the container the outer
-- block just created. Six containers of ninety-six wells, from one firing.
rule LayOut when ExperimentDesign {
    for each replicate from 1 to replicates, position from 1 to containerCount {
        Container from { design: this, replicate: replicate, position: position } as container
        for each condition in conditions, slot from 1 to wellsPerCondition {
            Well from {
                container: container
                condition: condition
                position: (condition.block - 1) * wellsPerCondition + slot
            }
        }
    }
}
